      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمُومَةٌ</span></b> . (S, M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمَمْتُهُ</span> <i>I was to him a mother.</i> (A in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ربض</span>.) IAar, speaking of a
woman, said, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَانَتْ لَهَا عَمَّةٌ تَؤُمُّهَا</span>, meaning [<i>She
had,</i> lit. <i>there was to her, a paternal aunt</i>] <i>who
was to her like the mother.</i> (M.)

